---
title: "Image"
description: "Places an image or video in the content, ported from Hugo's `{{< img >}}` shortcode."
type: static
---

Places an image or video in the content, wrapped in a `<figure>` by default. Images are served from `docs.dd-static.net`, with automatic `srcset` generation for 1x/2x pixel density.

## Properties

**Unused in Hugo:** The Hugo shortcode also supports `href`, `target`, `wide`, `img_param`, `pop_param`, `figure_class`, and `figure_style`, but none of these appear in any real usage across `hugo/content/en/`. They're omitted here as low-priority for porting; see the source templates linked above if they're ever needed.

| Property | Type | Default | Description |
|----------|------|---------|-------------|
| `src` | `string` | — | Required. Path to the image, relative to the site's images directory. |
| `alt` | `string` | — | Alt text for accessibility. |
| `caption` | `string` | — | Text displayed below the image in a `<figcaption>`. |
| `style` | `string` | — | Inline CSS applied to the image (and its wrapping `<picture>`). |
| `width` | `string` | — | Width attribute on the rendered `<img>`. |
| `height` | `string` | — | Height attribute on the rendered `<img>`. |
| `inline` | `boolean` | `false` | Renders a bare inline `<img>` (no figure wrapper, no popup, no srcset). |
| `video` | `boolean` | `false` | Renders `src` as an autoplaying, looping, muted `<video>` instead of an image. |
| `popup` | `boolean` | `true` | Wraps the image in a link that opens it full-size in a modal. |

**Note:** `video`, `inline`, and `popup` are evaluated in that priority order — for example, `video=true` takes precedence over `inline`.

